# Real sites whose pages are published as files, pinned, for
# tools/ref/corpus.py: fetched by a hash, served from this machine, the
# same bytes every run, with no site to reach and none to refuse a robot.
#
#	name archive URL sha256:HEX strip=DIR [only=PATH,PATH...]
#	name git URL COMMIT paths=PATH,PATH...
#
# An archive's hash is checked before it is opened; a git commit is
# fetched by its hash, which git checks every object against.  strip is
# the directory in the archive the site is (its root); only, the parts
# of it kept (a directory ends in /).  paths, a git source's sparse
# checkout.  A page names its files from the site's root (/docs/...),
# so each is served at a root of its own.
